WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.837
Undo and permission: what is actually protected.

2
00:00:03.117 --> 00:00:06.957
Claude Code has two safety mechanisms with very different scopes.

3
00:00:07.237 --> 00:00:17.157
Checkpoints snapshot a file before Claude’s file tools edit it, so pressing Escape twice (or /rewind ) can roll back code, conversation, or both.

4
00:00:17.437 --> 00:00:30.664
The checkpointing docs are explicit about the edges: files changed only by a Bash command aren’t restored, and actions on remote systems (databases, APIs, deployments) can’t be checkpointed at all.

5
00:00:30.944 --> 00:00:34.016
Checkpoints work alongside git; they don’t replace it.

6
00:00:34.296 --> 00:00:36.771
Permissions decide what runs without asking.

7
00:00:37.051 --> 00:00:51.003
At the time of writing, the modes are Manual (Claude asks before edits and non-read-only commands), Accept edits (file edits and common filesystem commands run freely), Plan (explore and propose, no source edits),

8
00:00:51.283 --> 00:01:04.253
Auto (a separate classifier model reviews actions and blocks risky ones), dontAsk (only pre-approved tools, for locked-down scripts), and bypassPermissions (everything, for isolated containers only).

9
00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:08.075
Recent versions start interactive sessions in Auto mode.

10
00:01:08.355 --> 00:01:15.800
The most useful idea in the best-practices doc is the split between non-deterministic and deterministic instructions.

11
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.253
Your prompt, CLAUDE.

12
00:01:17.533 --> 00:01:22.931
md, and skills are read by the model, which usually follows them but isn’t guaranteed to.

13
00:01:23.211 --> 00:01:30.827
Hooks, deny rules, the sandbox, and managed settings are executed by the harness every time, whatever the model decides.

14
00:01:31.107 --> 00:01:40.515
Auto mode sits in between: it’s a model making a judgment, which the docs caution can be wrong, so “never” rules belong in deny rules or hooks.

15
00:01:40.795 --> 00:01:43.205
Keep this split in mind for the whole elective.

16
00:01:43.485 --> 00:01:49.309
Every time you want something to always (or never) happen, ask which side of the line your control is on.
